   "mode": null,
   "preinstalled": {
    "zh": "上游锁定依赖（uv sync --frozen）加兼容补丁 compat.patch；TeX Live（含 fonts-extra、latexmk）；给 agent 用的研究 Python 环境 /opt/research",
    "en": "upstream's locked dependencies (uv sync --frozen) plus compat.patch; TeX Live (with fonts-extra and latexmk); a research Python environment for the agent in /opt/research"
   }
  },
  "roles": [],
  "world": null,
  "notes": {
   "agent": "No external coding agent: EvoScientist runs its own in-process planner/research/code/debug/writing sub-agents (LangChain deepagents) on the one configured model. conditions.agent only selects the provider; Claude Code and Codex are not used.",
   "model": "Main agent, sub-agents and EvoScientist's auxiliary calls (tool selector, memory workers, summariser, graders) all use the configured model; auxiliary_model and model_fallbacks are empty.",
   "effort": "For the OpenAI provider upstream already takes the effort from EVOSCIENTIST_REASONING_EFFORT (= conditions.effort) and sends it as reasoning.effort; compat.patch (Claude only) is not involved. No max_tokens is set, and codex-api removes max_output_tokens anyway.",
   "paper": "The core writes a Markdown report (final_report.md); the EvoSkills paper-writing skill gives a generic LaTeX `article` skeleton with no ICML/ICLR/NeurIPS style and no compile step. The image has TeX Live (latexmk, fonts-extra) but no venue style files; the task asks for an official template, so a venue-formatted PDF depends on the agent obtaining the style through the shield. No extra pipeline stage was added; absent items are listed in result.missing.",
   "tools": "skill_manager (git clone of any repository as a skill) is not registered (compat.patch); the Tavily key is not set so tavily_search does not exist; LANGGRAPH_CLI_NO_ANALYTICS=1; EvoSkills is baked in at its pinned commit. The execute shell and the EvoSkills paper-navigator scripts reach the world only through the shield; S2_DATE_CUTOFF is not set (the shield bounds dates).",
   "server_side_search": "Not reachable: EvoScientist binds no provider-side search tool to any model (its only tools are think_tool, tavily_search when TAVILY_API_KEY is set, MCP tools from mcp.yaml, deepagents built-ins and skills; EvoScientist/EvoScientist.py:671-672 and 754-755 at the pin; the one bind_tools call is the tool selector's own output schema, middleware/tool_selector.py:166). TAVILY_API_KEY is not passed and the image has no mcp.yaml, so no search tool exists. Anthropic/OpenAI hosts are only tunnelled by the shield, so a provider-side search would be invisible to the audit.",
   "credentials": "The container holds only a placeholder in OPENAI_API_KEY and EvoScientist's execute shell inherits it; the shield proxy puts codex-api's local key on the request and the login stays on the host.",
   "memory": "A fresh data dir per run (baked skills, empty memory). Memory workers, skill synthesis and the scheduler stay at upstream defaults, so their LLM calls count in the usage log.",
   "limits": "async sub-agents off (README advice for scripted runs); recursion_limit=1000000; model retry wait in auto-mode 1800 s (time without progress counts as wall time); execute timeout 300 s per command. No token or cost budget exists.",
   "model_access": "the project's own ChatGPT (Codex) login through codex-api  (account codex-2): EvoScientist's native OpenAI provider with its own OPENAI_BASE_URL set to codex-api; upstream sends reasoning={effort, summary: auto} for a GPT model (langchain-openai then uses the Responses API), with the effort from EVOSCIENTIST_REASONING_EFFORT (= conditions.effort); developer-role.patch (RWE_RESPONSES_DEVELOPER_ROLE=1) sends the system prompt as a `developer` message, because the ChatGPT Codex backend answers a `system` message in a Responses input with HTTP 400"
  },
